(11610, 120, 'Mohd Qaisar Moin', 'DOAGURU', 'Deployment', 'Deployment ', 'Dashboard & Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)\nDynamic Dashboard: We fixed the UI so that it dynamically shows or hides action cards (like \"Register Receptionist\" or \"New Consultation\") based on whether the logged-in user is a Doctor or a Receptionist.\nBackend Security: We implemented strict role verification on the backend. The API now inspects a user\'s token and automatically restricts access to sensitive endpoints (e.g., only Doctors can hit the /save consultation route).\nData Consistency: We ensured the authentication context always fetches fresh profile data on application load so the app doesn\'t stall on stale temporary state.\n2. Live Patient Records Integration\nDatabase Switch: We successfully migrated the \"Patient Records\" list away from the fake dummy_patients.json file. It is now fully wired up to your live MySQL database, meaning it instantly reflects real registered patients and powers the search bar using live database queries.\n3. Vitals & Contact Editing Feature\nLive Editing UI: We built the functionality allowing Receptionists to edit a patient\'s Contact Information and Vitals directly from the slide-out panel in the Patient Records screen.\nComplex Database Mapping: We solved the schema challenge where Contact Info belongs to the patients table, but Vitals belong inside a specific consultations row.\nEditing Contact Info updates the patients table directly via a PUT request.\nEditing Vitals checks if an active consultation exists today. If yes, it updates it. If no, we built logic to automatically generate a placeholder consultation just to securely hold those Vitals!\nUI Bug Fix: We caught and fixed a bug where the Patient Detail panel would momentarily flash blank after saving Vitals by ensuring the React state merges the new data cleanly on the fly.\nEverything is now securely connected to the database and saving data correctly!\n', '0', '0', 480, 0, '2026-02-23', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
