(11876, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'Learning ', 'Development', 'Back-End', 'Today I communicated with the Natura client and shared the Requirement Document, which includes the necessary details for updating and modifying the website content as per their requirements.\nI also started reviewing the sf.duaguru software codebase to understand its working structure. I primarily focused on the backend section. While analyzing the code, I was able to understand some parts, but certain sections—particularly the userRouter and itemController—are quite complex and require deeper analysis. The code structure appears to be less modular, with many functionalities placed within a single file, making it comparatively harder to understand.', '0', '0', 522, 0, '2026-03-14', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
